max-visits: 6
go-to: labor_rights_menu

= Workers' Rights

With the labour ministry, we can set national standards for work. Our supporters expect a higher minimum wage, more workers covered by collective agreements, and protection for the people who deliver our parcels and food.

@labor_rights_menu

- @working_hours: Raise the minimum wage and strengthen collective agreements.
- @shorten_hours: Support a shorter working week.
- @safety: Protect platform and delivery workers.
- @root: Do not enact any policies.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@working_hours
view-if: working_hours < 2
on-arrival: working_hours += 1; labor_dissent -= 8; left_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 5; workers_spd += 7*(1-dissent); fdp_relation -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if fdp_relation <= 30; labor_goal_completed = 1; inflation += 0.1; economic_growth -= 0.1

[? if working_hours == 1 : The minimum wage rises to 15 euros, following the EU directive's benchmark of 60% of the median wage. ?][? if working_hours >= 2 : Public contracts now go only to companies that pay union rates, and collective agreements are easier to extend to a whole sector. ?] The employers' associations warn of job losses, and the unions celebrate.

@shorten_hours
view-if: working_hours >= 2
subtitle: Could shorter hours keep people in work and attract skilled workers?
on-arrival: working_hours += 1; labor_dissent -= 8; left_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 5; workers_spd += 7*(1-dissent); fdp_relation -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; labor_goal_completed = 1; unemployment_rate -= 0.2 if recession_seen = 1; economic_growth -= 0.2;

We fund pilot projects for a four-day week and give workers a right to reduce their hours and return to full time. IG Metall has wanted this for years. Employers say that Germany cannot afford to work less when skilled workers are already scarce.

@safety
on-arrival: workers_safety += 1; labor_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 2; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1 if workers_safety >= 3

[? if workers_safety == 1 : Delivery platforms must now employ their riders, not treat them as self-employed. ?][? if workers_safety == 2 : Parcel companies can no longer hide behind chains of subcontractors, and heavy parcels must be carried by two people. ?][? if workers_safety >= 3 : We strengthen the labour inspectorate and protection against heat at work. Business groups begin to complain about too much regulation. ?]
